# 28 — Previous arrangements and open decisions

[Plan](plan.md) · [Tasks](tasks.md)

## Planning evidence

**Scope decision:** Pending — The actual successor entity and treatment of existing beneficiaries have not been approved. Next: obtain owner decisions informed by a source-backed reconstruction and qualified counsel.

**Prior art:** [Original Banodoco ownership proposal](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/index.html) documents the historical monthly distribution and a proposed, explicitly provisional structure; [grant records](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/data.js) contain named monthly recipients. [Equity Review](https://github.com/banodoco/equity-review/blob/5319eadcabe319e6de646b09ed2b6b3bda4e829a/README.md) describes a three-stage contribution shortlist/review. The public sources don't prove executed equity transfers, recipient assent or a complete cap table.

**Approach:** Preserve and reconcile historic publications and direct promises first; then compare a successor to the old mechanism against alternative legal vehicles. Do not treat either the old percentage schedule or a new distribution algorithm as predetermined.

**Challenge:** Pending — Existing recipient expectations and promises, investment, governance, employment and tax have material consequences. Next: independent legal/tax and fairness review before any binding decision.

**Proof and limits:** Pending — Actual instruments and individual commitments have not been reconciled. Next: audit sources, verify ambiguities with recipients, qualify legal terms, and define executable proof and appeal cases.

## What to verify before deciding

- Published model: a 1%-per-month approach for 8.5 years, across evolving contributor categories, with disclaimers about legal setup and dilution. Document the actual terms at each relevant date; **do not infer uniform allocations to each named person**.
- Prior awards: dated lists, transfers and directly communicated terms may differ. Keep individual evidence with provenance, private when appropriate; investigate duplicates, aliases, changes over time and claims that are missing from public lists.
- Entity boundary: was a grant of Banodoco, an existing legal company, a future vehicle, or an economic promise? How would any rights and obligations carry into the Astrid/Mycelial collective, and how do external investors affect them?
- New mechanism: who can earn participation, how creative and open-source contributions are evaluated, review/appeal independence, allocation cadence, dilution, lockups, funding, governance and participant communications.

Sources: [ownership explanation](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/index.html) · [published grants](https://github.com/banodoco/Banodoco-website/blob/e46641b15f99d9bc26788039c96944e06ffc32b6/ownership/data.js) · [review tool](https://github.com/banodoco/equity-review/blob/5319eadcabe319e6de646b09ed2b6b3bda4e829a/README.md) · [community-data tools](https://github.com/banodoco/brain-of-bndc/blob/740832a406770bcf011ef33bd2aea371074564ea/README.md) · [CA-002](../../vision/gaps/CA-002-contributor-ownership.md).

These publications are historical evidence, not proof that any particular equity right is legally operative.
